<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kęstutis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1297–<a href="/years/1382">1382</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Kestutis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kęstutis was a Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediminas">Gediminas</a> who ruled the western lands of Lithuania from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trakai">Trakai</a> from the 1340s. For decades he shared power with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a>, defending Lithuania against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> while Algirdas expanded into Rus'. He seized the throne from his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a> in 1381 but was captured by him and died in prison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kreva">Kreva</a> in 1382.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kestutis.jpg" alt="Kęstutis" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_K%C4%99stutis,_1379.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
